+/* Windows lets a running thread keep the processor until it blocks, gives it
+ * up (Sleep(0), SwitchToThread) or uses up its quantum. Handing the machine
+ * over at every import while another thread waited switched threads at
+ * nearly every import: a thread holding a lock that another spins on with no
+ * import in its loop was switched out mid-section, and the spinning thread
+ * then ran its loop until a back edge handed the machine back. An import or
+ * a back edge now hands the machine over only once the running thread has
+ * passed a quantum of hand-over points (imports and back-edge hooks) since it
+ * took the machine; a wait, a Sleep and Sleep(0) still hand it over at once.
+ * The quantum is counted in the guest's own steps, never in host time. A loop
+ * that has run RECOMP_YIELD_EVERY back edges without calling a single import
+ * is spinning (or computing) on its own: on the multiprocessor machines the
+ * game ran on, the thread it waits for ran meanwhile, so that back edge hands
+ * the machine to a waiter at once, inside the quantum or not. */
+#ifndef HLE_QUANTUM_POINTS
+#define HLE_QUANTUM_POINTS 1024u        /* about 0.3 to 1 ms of the game's imports here */
+#endif
+unsigned hle_quantum_points = HLE_QUANTUM_POINTS;  /* a test sets its own */
+static unsigned g_points;               /* hand-over points since the last take */
